{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And from Bamoth in the valley that is in the field of Moab.</b> For there Moses died, and there the Well ceased. Another interpretation: ״the nobles of the people dug״ — every prince, when they would encamp, would take his staff and draw a line alongside his standard and camp, and the waters of the Well would be drawn through that sign and come before the encampment of every tribe (Tanchuma)." "<b>at the lawgiver.</b> By the mouth of Moses, who is called lawgiver, as it says ״for there the portion of the lawgiver is hidden״ (Deuteronomy 33). And why is Moses not mentioned in this song? Because he was punished on account of the Well — and since the name of Moses is not mentioned, the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, is not mentioned either. A parable: a king who was invited to a banquet — he said, If my friend is there, I am there; and if not, I do not go (Tanchuma)." "<b>the top of the peak.</b> As the Targum renders: ״רֵישׁ רָמָתָא.״" "<b>peak.</b> A term of height, and likewise ״פַּסְּגוּ אַרְמְנוֹתֶיהָ״ (Psalms 48) — raise high its palaces." "<b>and looked out.</b> That peak looked out over the face of the place whose name is Jeshimon — and that is a term for wilderness, which is desolate. Another interpretation: ״and the Well looked out over the face of the wasteland״ — for it was hidden in the Sea of Tiberias, and one who stands over the wasteland looks and sees something like a sieve in the sea, and that is the Well. So Rabbi Tanchuma expounded."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:05.337233768Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}